diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -99,6 +99,35 @@
 Use `-h` on an executable to list every numerical, solver, output, and
 time-stepping option.
 
+## Two-dimensional verification data
+
+Both 2D executables accept `-theta0 30` to start from a smooth parabolic
+droplet with an initial 30° contact angle. The separate `-theta`
+option sets the Young angle and `-zeta` sets diffuse contact-line friction.
+Use `-cap-init` to start from a circular cap. In that mode the initial angle
+defaults to the Young angle. The original rectangular initialization is the
+default.
+
+The smooth initial fields interpolate `tanh(d/(sqrt(2)*delta))` in the Q1
+space, where `d` is signed Euclidean distance to the parabola or circle
+extended through the substrate. The prescribed half-domain liquid area is
+`0.125`, so the target phase-field mass is `0.75`. A tapered nodal adjustment
+in the appropriate bulk phase matches this mass. The adjustment leaves every
+element intersected by the Q1 zero contour unchanged.
+
+The Q1 solvers write `geometry.csv` at initialization and after each accepted
+step. Its columns report time, step, the outermost zero crossing on the
+substrate, the one-sided Q1 contact angle in degrees, the highest zero crossing
+on the symmetry axis, and `sqrt(2)*delta*|grad(phi)|` at the contact point.
+The local angle and profile scale use the gradient from the adjacent bulk
+element. Use `-no-geom` to disable these diagnostics.
+
+The common visualization times `0.02`, `0.2`, and `1.0` are reached by shortening
+steps that would cross them, including in fixed-step mode. For a time
+refinement study, use a final time and step sizes commensurate with these
+fixed output times. Use `-edrtol -1` to disable early stopping, and check the
+accepted step sizes in `time_specialized.csv`.
+
 ## Reproduce the paper figures
 
 Set short names for the output directories:
